# Example .raytrainignore
#
# Copy to .raytrainignore at the repo root. Same syntax as .gitignore.
# Patterns here are *added on top of* raytrain's built-in defaults
# (.git/, __pycache__/, data/, *.ckpt, etc.) and any .gitignore in the repo.
#
# Anything matched here is excluded from the code zip uploaded to MinIO
# when you run `raytrain submit`.
#
# Use it for things specific to your project that built-in defaults don't
# catch:

# experiment outputs unique to your project
outputs/
runs/
results/

# big artifacts you don't want shipped
*.onnx
*.bin

# auto-generated docs / coverage
htmlcov/
docs/_build/

# weights & biases / tensorboard
wandb/
mlruns/
events.out.tfevents.*

# data files specific to the repo
*.parquet
*.feather
